{
  "about": "What a building's parts can be (docs/design/builders.md section 4; Buildings.cs). Rows, like every table: a mod adds or replaces one whole under \"buildings\". What's under \"look\" is the view's and stays out of Rules.Fingerprint; the rest decides cells. A building's own rows are world data: world/buildings.json, the villages (world/villages.json), or a mod's \"world\" section.",
  "ground": "dirt",
  "drawn": {
    "about": "What the view reads of a building (RowMesher, RowHouses). A row's \"level\" stands its walls from the highest ground under it, running them down to the lowest, so their tops are one height; a tower's height and a wall's count from there, kept in step with it by hand: anything else a row, wall, opening or parts row says is kept but never drawn, and validate and apply say so. A roof's fields are its shape's look.takes, a part's its detail's. An opening's look \"lamp\" is the colour its pane glows from dusk to dawn (\"#rrggbb\", brighter the lighter; \"off\" for none), and an opening in a row may give its own; the glass goes dark when its pane breaks or its stretch of wall burns or falls. On a building the cells' own looks aren't drawn: the house draws each opening from its row here, and only a pane cell shows glass that breaks.",
    "row": ["id", "at", "style", "seed", "storeys", "fill", "floor", "wall", "joins", "walls", "roofs", "parts", "built", "site", "level", "towers", "roads"],
    "floor": ["kind", "height"],
    "wall": ["from", "to", "material", "height", "thickness", "finish", "storey", "openings"],
    "finish": ["color", "pattern"],
    "opening": ["kind", "at", "width", "shape", "finish", "lamp"],
    "openingLook": ["width", "height", "sill", "lamp"],
    "style": ["fill", "floor", "wall", "storeys", "roof", "parts", "recipe"],
    "tower": ["at", "radius", "material", "height", "roof"]
  },
